\newsection{Competitive Programming}

If you've used sites like LeetCode or HackerRank, you'll have noticed some of these problems are familiar.

For those of you not acquainted with these sites, they are places where you can find problems like the ones you may have solved in this document. There are a \textbf{lot} of different kinds of solutions to even the simplest problems.

Some companies actually take questions from these sites and use them in interviews, so not all of the aspects of competitive programming are just for the sake of programming.

Try out both the sample questions below to get used to the interface as you could end up using it a lot some day:

\href{https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum/}{Two Sum - LeetCode}\\\\\\

\href{https://www.hackerrank.com/challenges/solve-me-first/problem}{Solve Me First - HackerRank}\\\\\\

After you're done with that, go explore! There are thousands of problems on these sites so you'll almost never run out of things to do.
